# =============================================================================
# Aether — Environment Variable Template
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values. NEVER commit `.env`.
#   cp .env.example .env
# `.env` is git-ignored. Do not paste real secrets into `.env.example`.
# =============================================================================

# ---- AI / LLM providers ----
# OpenRouter is the PER-AGENT opt-in gateway ONLY — the 22-agent model picker
# routes a run there when (and only when) an agent's stored config names a slash
# (vendor/model) id. It is NEVER the system default or an automatic fallback
# (OWNER DIRECTIVE, 2026-08-14). Leave the key blank unless you use the picker.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=your-openrouter-api-key-here
OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# System-default model tiers used by the agent layer. Each is a BARE claude-*
# id served by the operator's Anthropic Pro subscription (resolve_provider ->
# 'anthropic'); a '/' in an id would route to OpenRouter, so a tier default must
# NEVER contain one. These mirror llm_client._DEFAULT_MODEL_BY_TIER so behaviour
# is Anthropic-first even when a var is unset. Override PER AGENT via the picker,
# not here. Phase 2 tiers: reasoning (planning/complex), fast (general),
# structured (JSON extraction), light (cheap classification / smoke checks).
# AUD-ECON-2 (RUN-20260818T0223Z): REASONING was claude-opus-4-8; every real
# prod tailor/coverLetter run was actually served by claude-haiku-4-5 via the
# existing fallback chain, and Opus at published prices costs ~7x today's real
# spend (~$1.70/application vs ~$0.24), blowing the Free plan's spend cap on a
# single tailoring run. The default now matches what the product actually
# serves and can afford — set this var to re-pin Opus with no code change.
# Full rationale: docs/delivery/evidence/RUN-20260818T0223Z/AUD-ECON-2/
# 03-implementation-rationale.md.
AETHER_MODEL_REASONING=claude-haiku-4-5
AETHER_MODEL_FAST=claude-haiku-4-5
AETHER_MODEL_STRUCTURED=claude-sonnet-4-6
AETHER_MODEL_LIGHT=claude-haiku-4-5
# Legacy alias kept for Phase 1 scripts (heavy == reasoning, opus-class) — NOT
# updated by AUD-ECON-2: no current backend runs on the HEAVY tier, and the
# decision above is scoped to REASONING (tailor/coverLetter) specifically.
AETHER_MODEL_HEAVY=claude-opus-4-8
# Fallback model tried ONCE when a SYSTEM-DEFAULT primary fails/times out (ADR
# D-0017 / D-0014). A bare claude-* on the SAME Anthropic subscription — never a
# cross-provider substitution. It is DISTINCT from the reasoning/heavy tier
# (opus -> haiku one-retry), which is where the retry earns its keep; when the
# primary already IS this id (the fast/light haiku tiers) _model_chain collapses
# to a single call, so a same-model no-op retry never happens. A user-CHOSEN
# model is never silently replaced by this fallback (ADR-ML-3).
AETHER_MODEL_FALLBACK=claude-haiku-4-5
# ADMIN-ONLY rescue chain for an OpenRouter HTTP 402 (insufficient credits).
# Comma-separated FREE ($0-priced) model ids. When a live call 402s and the run
# belongs to the admin account (User.isAdmin = true), the model chain continues
# with these so the owner's pipeline keeps producing — OpenRouter's 402 gate is
# per-model-price, not account-wide, so $0-priced models still answer on a
# zero-credit key. Every other user is unaffected (honest 503, quota refunded).
# The free catalog churns: re-verify these ids before relying on them. Leave the
# value EMPTY to disable the rescue entirely. Unset = the two live-verified
# defaults below (probe 2026-07-29,
# uat/reports/evidence/free-model-fallback/PROBE-REPORT.json).
AETHER_ADMIN_FREE_FALLBACK_MODELS=nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free,nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free
# Optional provider override: point the agent layer at any OpenAI-compatible
# endpoint (e.g. Anthropic's https://api.anthropic.com/v1 with an Anthropic API
# key and Claude model ids in the AETHER_MODEL_* vars). When unset, OpenRouter
# (OPENROUTER_BASE_URL/OPENROUTER_API_KEY) is used.
AETHER_LLM_BASE_URL=
AETHER_LLM_API_KEY=
# Extra HTTP headers (JSON object) sent on every live LLM call. Required by
# Anthropic's OpenAI-compat endpoint, e.g.:
# AETHER_LLM_EXTRA_HEADERS={"anthropic-version":"2023-06-01","anthropic-beta":"oauth-2025-04-20"}
# (the anthropic-beta header is only needed for OAuth/subscription tokens)
AETHER_LLM_EXTRA_HEADERS=
# Claude Code OAuth token (GAP-P7-DEF-A). Written HERE automatically by the
# server when a user saves a `claude setup-token` credential (sk-ant-oat01-…) in
# the Agents → Configure Anthropic modal; oauth_token runs bill against the
# Claude Pro/Max subscription. Do NOT paste secrets into this example file —
# the real value lands in the gitignored repo-root .env (600 perms). Override the
# target path with AETHER_ENV_FILE_PATH if the repo lives elsewhere.
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
# LLM record/replay mode for agent tests: replay (default, offline, no key),
# record (call live model + save fixture), auto (replay if present else record),
# or live (always call the live model). CI runs `replay`; only `record`/`auto`/
# `live` need OPENROUTER_API_KEY.
# SAFETY: the API refuses to start (RuntimeError, §REC-04) if AETHER_LLM_MODE
# is left at its `replay` default while AETHER_ENV=production — that combo
# would silently serve canned fixtures instead of real model output. Set this
# to `auto`, `live`, or `record` in production.
AETHER_LLM_MODE=replay

# Deployment environment: `development` (default) or `production`. This value
# GATES THE FIXTURE/REPLAY-MODE FAIL-FAST GUARD: when AETHER_ENV=production the
# API refuses to start (RuntimeError, §REC-04) if AETHER_LLM_MODE is still at
# its `replay` default — so production can never silently serve canned fixtures
# instead of real model output. Keep this at `development` in a copied local
# `.env` (the `replay` default is fine there); on the PRODUCTION deploy set
# `AETHER_ENV=production` AND `AETHER_LLM_MODE=auto|live|record`. Does not change
# app behavior otherwise.
AETHER_ENV=development

# Optional direct provider keys (fallbacks / specific agents)
OPENAI_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
GOOGLE_API_KEY=
GROQ_API_KEY=

# ---- Google OAuth (Gmail integration, P4) ----
# Create an OAuth 2.0 Client (type: Web application) in Google Cloud Console,
# enable the Gmail API, add scopes gmail.modify / gmail.send / gmail.labels +
# openid / email / profile, and register the redirect URI below as an authorized
# redirect URI. While the app is in "testing", add yourself as a test user.
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Must EXACTLY match an authorized redirect URI on the OAuth client. In prod:
# https://<your-host>/api/auth/google/callback  (nginx proxies /api/* → FastAPI).
GOOGLE_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI=
# OPTIONAL. Dedicated secret for signing the short-lived OAuth `state` token.
# Left unset, it derives from NEXTAUTH_SECRET but is namespaced so it can never
# equal the app session-signing secret — a state token can never be replayed as
# a session token. Set this only to fully isolate the two key materials.
GOOGLE_OAUTH_STATE_SECRET=

# ---- Database ----
# Hosted PostgreSQL. When the provider only grants a single database, use
# separate schemas for dev/test via Prisma's `?schema=` parameter.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host:5432/dbname?schema=aether&connect_timeout=15"
# Separate test database/schema for integration tests (repository tests skip if unset).
DATABASE_URL_TEST="postgresql://user:password@host:5432/dbname?schema=aether_test&connect_timeout=15"

# ---- Queue (BullMQ / Redis) ----
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379

# ---- Vector store (semantic search / embeddings) ----
PINECONE_API_KEY=
PINECONE_INDEX=aether

# ---- Auth (NextAuth) ----
NEXTAUTH_SECRET=change-me
NEXTAUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000

# ---- Web app ----
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000

# ---- Operator legal identity / support contact (MV-terms-002/003,
# MV-privacy-policy-003; H-3, operator-held, BLOCKED-ON-HUMAN) ----
# Read server-side, at request time, by the public /terms and /privacy-policy
# pages (apps/web/src/lib/config/legal.ts). Leaving these unset is honest and
# safe: the pages render a truthful "not yet configured" statement instead of
# a placeholder or a fabricated value — set them once the operator has real
# values, then restart aether-web.service (docs/delivery/DEPLOYMENT-RUNBOOK.md).
# Defaults to "Aether" if unset.
AETHER_OPERATOR_BUSINESS_NAME=
# The operating entity's registered Australian Business Number. No default —
# required for GST tax invoices to be legally complete; shown on /terms §5.
AETHER_OPERATOR_ABN=
# A real, monitored support inbox shown as a mailto: link on /terms §18 and
# /privacy-policy §7 (refunds, account closure, data export/deletion, GST
# invoice questions). No default — do not set this to an address nobody reads.
AETHER_SUPPORT_EMAIL=

# ---- Outbound transactional email (O-4 password reset) ----
# See docs/delivery/EMAIL-SETUP.md for the 5-minute operator setup. Set EITHER
# the SMTP group OR AETHER_EMAIL_API_KEY (SMTP wins if both are set) — leaving
# both unset is honest and safe: POST /auth/forgot-password still 200s (never
# a broken flow), it just cannot deliver a reset link, and the UI says so.
AETHER_SMTP_HOST=
AETHER_SMTP_PORT=587
AETHER_SMTP_USER=
AETHER_SMTP_PASS=
AETHER_SMTP_FROM=
# Resend-style HTTPS email API, used only when AETHER_SMTP_HOST is unset.
AETHER_EMAIL_API_KEY=
AETHER_EMAIL_FROM=

# ---- API app ----
API_HOST=0.0.0.0
API_PORT=8000

# ---- Internal-use email allowlist (GAP-P7-DEF-B / §15) ----
# Comma-separated internal domains to allow in email validation. Without
# this, pydantic's EmailStr (via email-validator) rejects any domain in its
# reserved Special-Use list (.local, .test, .onion, .arpa, .invalid,
# "localhost") regardless of check_deliverability — e.g. a stored/seeded
# admin@aether.local account cannot save its own settings. Only the exact
# domain(s) listed here are opened; every other special-use domain stays
# rejected.
AETHER_ALLOWED_INTERNAL_EMAIL_DOMAINS=aether.local

# ---- Observability (optional) ----
LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY=
LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY=

# ---- Job board sources (Phase 2 discovery agents) ----
SEEK_BASE_URL=https://www.seek.com.au
LINKEDIN_BASE_URL=https://www.linkedin.com/jobs
INDEED_BASE_URL=https://au.indeed.com

# ---- NLP / embeddings (Phase 2 matching) ----
SENTENCE_TRANSFORMERS_HOME=/tmp/aether_models
SPACY_MODEL=en_core_web_sm

# ---- Async background generation (GAP-P7-ASYNC-001, Phase 7) ----
# Code default OFF. Flip to true only after the J3 soak (see
# deploy/PHASE7-ASYNC-DEPLOY.md). When OFF, run endpoints stay synchronous 200.
AETHER_ASYNC_GENERATION=false
# Redis password (openssl rand -hex 24) + URL on a dedicated logical DB (3).
AETHER_REDIS_PASSWORD=
AETHER_REDIS_URL=redis://:CHANGE_ME@127.0.0.1:6379/3
# Worker-side LLM budgets (seconds) — more generous than the HTTP edge budgets;
# MUST stay below the ARQ job_timeout (600s).
AETHER_LLM_WORKER_BUDGET_SECONDS=300
AETHER_LLM_WORKER_COVER_BUDGET_SECONDS=300
AETHER_LLM_WORKER_PIPELINE_BUDGET_SECONDS=480
# Watchdog: mark a job failed+refunded if stuck past this many seconds (enqueued;
# processing window = this - 180). Default 900 (15 min).
AETHER_JOB_STALE_SECONDS=900

# ---- Abandoned-AgentRun watchdog (CRITICAL-1) ----
# AETHER_JOB_STALE_SECONDS above covers BackgroundJob. These cover AgentRun —
# the row the dashboard renders. Production had ONE tailor AgentRun stuck at
# status='running' for 8 days (2026-07-26 -> 2026-08-03) because nothing ever
# reconciled it, and the UI kept calling it an ACTIVE run.
#
# An executing run stamps AgentRun.heartbeatAt every INTERVAL seconds. A run is
# reconciled (failed, with an honest "Run abandoned - no worker heartbeat"
# error; never deleted, never faked 'completed') ONLY when the liveness evidence
# is missing: a heartbeat stale by more than STALE_SECONDS, or NO heartbeat ever
# recorded AND older than MAX_SECONDS. A live run keeps stamping, so it is never
# reaped on age alone however long it legitimately runs.
#
# MAX_SECONDS default 1800 is derived from real observed durations, not guessed:
# across 3,984 completed production runs the longest ever completed was 403.4s
# (fitScorer) and the worst per-agent p95 was 289.7s (tailor), while ARQ's own
# hard ceilings are job_timeout=600s / board-sweep 900s. 1800s is 4.5x the
# longest completed run and 2x ARQ's largest hard timeout. Values below 900 are
# clamped up so a misconfiguration cannot reap live work.
AETHER_AGENT_RUN_MAX_SECONDS=1800
AETHER_AGENT_RUN_HEARTBEAT_STALE_SECONDS=300      # 10 missed 30s stamps
AETHER_AGENT_RUN_HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL_SECONDS=30
AETHER_AGENT_RUN_STARTUP_STALE_SECONDS=120        # tighter, used at API/worker boot

# ---- Continuous board-sweep autopilot (RT-007) ----
# Code default OFF. When ON, an ARQ cron (every 10 min) enqueues one BOUNDED
# per-user sweep stretch that tailors + drafts cover letters for EVERY eligible
# job (scored / stuck-at-tailoring, with no Application yet) via the same
# reserved-run quota machinery manual runs use — so users never hand-run agents
# and one run no longer stops at a single tailored résumé. Every artifact still
# lands behind the existing human-approval gate. Quota exhaustion (429) ends the
# stretch honestly. Requires AETHER_ASYNC_GENERATION=true (shares the worker).
AETHER_BOARD_SWEEP_ENABLED=false
AETHER_BOARD_SWEEP_STRETCH_SECONDS=540   # ~10-min operator stretch; floored at 60
AETHER_BOARD_SWEEP_MAX_JOBS=10           # jobs processed per stretch
AETHER_BOARD_SWEEP_MAX_USERS=20          # users enqueued per 10-min tick

# ---- Entailment (anti-fabrication) verifier budget (GAP-P6-TAIL-004/005) ----
# The verifier runs in its OWN fresh window so a slow tailor generation can't
# starve it into reverting every genuine edit (RT-002). Keep >= ~15s.
AETHER_LLM_ENTAILMENT_BUDGET_SECONDS=20
AETHER_LLM_ENTAILMENT_BUDGET_PER_CANDIDATE_SECONDS=2.5
AETHER_LLM_ENTAILMENT_BUDGET_MAX_SECONDS=40

# ---- Adzuna AU licensed aggregator (RT-003, operator-held free credentials) ----
# Absent -> the adapter honestly SKIPS (no fabrication); present -> real AU job
# volume (the ToS-compliant path to Seek-advertised roles). Register free at
# https://developer.adzuna.com/ . See docs/delivery/LAUNCH-READY-BLOCKED-ON-HUMAN.md.
ADZUNA_APP_ID=
ADZUNA_APP_KEY=

# Optional: Market vs. You benchmark cache TTL in seconds (D-0042). Clamped to
# [60, 21600]; max 21600 = 6h benchmark cache TTL, the ToS-safe ceiling before
# a "market data as of" label would misdescribe a job market that moves daily.
# Unset or out-of-range values fall back to the 21600s (6h) default.
AETHER_ADZUNA_BENCH_TTL_SECONDS=

# ---- Discovery cron system-run exemption (ADR-P7-05 / GAP-P7-DISCOVERY-001) ----
# Shared secret scripts/discovery_cron.sh sends as the X-Aether-System-Run
# header so the API can bypass ONLY the subscription-paywall check (never any
# other guard), and ONLY for the discovery pipeline's own scout/fit-scorer
# calls -- never any other agent. Leave unset to disable the exemption
# entirely (the header is then ignored, not a bypass-by-omission). NEVER
# commit a real value here: the deployer generates a fresh random secret
# (e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`) at deploy time and sets it only in the real
# `.env` (600 permissions, never logged).
#
# S-FIX-A / S-1: this secret is ALSO what authenticates the multi-subscriber
# discovery sweep (POST /agents/discovery/sweep) that scripts/discovery_cron.sh
# now calls. With it set, EVERY entitled subscriber gets scheduled discovery;
# with it unset the cron falls back to the legacy single-account path and no
# other subscriber gets automatic discovery. Set it in production.
AETHER_SYSTEM_RUN_SECRET=

# ---- Multi-subscriber discovery sweep (S-FIX-A / S-1) ----
# Max subscribers served per sweep tick (default 25) and the pause between
# users (default 5s), so N subscribers cannot burst the shared Adzuna budget
# or the hosted DB's 25-connection ceiling. Non-positive values fall back to
# the defaults -- there is deliberately no way to switch the bounds off.
AETHER_DISCOVERY_SWEEP_USER_CAP=
AETHER_DISCOVERY_SWEEP_SPACING_SECONDS=

# ---- Adzuna discovery-path scale guards (S-FIX-A / S-2) ----
# The free-tier key allows 25 calls/min and 250 calls/DAY for the WHOLE
# deployment, shared by every subscriber.
#   *_CACHE_TTL_SECONDS  response-cache TTL for a normalized (what/where/
#                        filters,page) search (default 14400 = 4h). Job
#                        listings are refreshed upstream on a multi-hour
#                        cadence, so 4h buys real sharing between overlapping
#                        subscriber searches without claiming freshness the
#                        upstream data does not have. An entry past its TTL is
#                        kept (up to 24h) purely as honest stale-serve material
#                        for the budget-exhausted path.
#   *_DAILY_BUDGET       calls/day the discovery path may spend (default 250).
#   *_BUDGET_SAFETY_MARGIN  held back from that for the separate salary
#                        benchmark path + operator probes (default 25).
# At budget the adapter serves cached listings stamped with their REAL fetch
# time and, when it holds nothing for that search, records an honest per-source
# "blocked" state ("quota resets at 00:00 UTC") -- never a silent empty result.
AETHER_ADZUNA_CACHE_TTL_SECONDS=
AETHER_ADZUNA_DAILY_BUDGET=
AETHER_ADZUNA_BUDGET_SAFETY_MARGIN=

# ---- Manual Sync cooldown (S-FIX-A / S-7) ----
# Per-user sliding window on POST /agents/scout/run (default 3 runs / 600s).
# Scout is deterministic and unmetered, so nothing else caps how fast one user
# can spend the shared Adzuna budget. Scheduled/system runs are exempt.
AETHER_SCOUT_SYNC_MAX_RUNS=
AETHER_SCOUT_SYNC_WINDOW_SECONDS=
